# The build context is the repo root (docker/Dockerfile, docker/compose.yaml, CI).
#
# `.git` is NOT excluded, deliberately: setuptools_scm shells out to `git describe`
# during `uv sync`'s build step, and without the tag history every image — and so
# every sidecar and every ledger row it produces — gets a placeholder `0.1.dev1+…`
# version instead of a real one (§12).
#
# README.md is NOT excluded either: pyproject.toml's `readme = {file = "README.md"}`
# is read at build time, and the build fails outright without it.
#
# Everything below is either irrelevant to the image or actively harmful. The
# integration cache is the one that matters most: a populated `.cache` makes the
# context ~2.2 GB, all of which is hashed and sent to the daemon on every local
# build. CI never noticed — the cache is restored in the smoke job, after the image
# is built — so this only ever hurt whoever built the image on their own machine.

.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
tests/integration/.cache/

# Local scratch and generated artefacts.
scratch/
dist/
site/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Nothing in the image reads these, and the image is not where they are consumed.
.github/
docs/
